<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06RW">Corollary <span data-tag="06RW">4.7.9.21</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer and suppose we are given a pullback diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@C =50pt@R=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{01} \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1 \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}. } \]
</div>
<p> If the lower horizontal map exhibits $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ as a homotopy $n$-category of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{1}$, then the upper horizontal map induces an isomorphism $\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{01})}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0)}}$. </p>
</article>
